<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Raj</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Raj, Indian Raj</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Raj was the system of direct British crown rule over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a> from 1858 to 1947, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>'s rule ended following the rebellion of 1857. It was headed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> and administered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-civil-service">Indian Civil Service</a>. The Raj was the centrepiece of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s independence in 1947 marked the beginning of its dissolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-raj.jpg" alt="British Raj" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edinburgh Geographical Institute; J. G. Bartholomew and Sons. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Indian_Empire_1909_Imperial_Gazetteer_of_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
